{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: When history shows a recent peak followed by a decline (e.g., >90 to <85), the model's flat or slightly rising forecast significantly overestimates future prices; apply a downward adjustment of 5-10 EUR to align with the observed mean reversion.",
    "Correct for upward bias after spikes: When history ends near a local high (e.g., >90) and sentiment is neutral/low, the model underestimates immediate upside momentum; increase the first 5-10 days of the forecast by 2-4 EUR to capture the initial breakout before mean reversion.",
    "Adjust for lag in volatility: The model fails to capture the amplitude of price swings, smoothing peaks and troughs; flatten the forecast slope and increase variance to match the true outcome's oscillation pattern.",
    "Incorporate sentiment lag: Neutral sentiment (0.00) during high volatility periods indicates the model ignores latent market stress; if sentiment history shows intermittent spikes (0.20-0.40) preceding a trend, weight the forecast more heavily toward the direction of the most recent sentiment spike rather than the historical mean.",
    "Horizon-specific correction: For horizons beyond 15 days, the model's convergence to a static mean is inaccurate; extend the trend direction of the first 10 days into the long-term forecast rather than reverting to the historical average."
  ]
}
